        <!-- Section: Negative Numbers & Imaginary -->
        <section class="article-section" id="section-negative-numbers">
            <div class="article-container">
                <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m12 3-1.9 5.8a2 2 0 0 1-1.3 1.3L3 12l5.8 1.9a2 2 0 0 1 1.3 1.3L12 21l1.9-5.8a2 2 0 0 1 1.3-1.3L21 12l-5.8-1.9a2 2 0 0 1-1.3-1.3z"/></svg></span> Complex Numbers</div>
                <h2 class="article-h2">Square Roots of Negative Numbers and Imaginary Unit</h2>
                <p>In the real number system, the square root of a negative number does not exist as a real value. By defining the imaginary unit <strong>i = √(−1)</strong>, we can express:</p>
                <div class="math-block"><span class="math-formula">√(−x) = i√x</span></div>

                <div class="table-scroll-wrapper">
                    <div class="table-scroll-hint">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 8L22 12L18 16"/><path d="M6 8L2 12L6 16"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/></svg>
                        Scroll horizontally →
                    </div>
                    <table class="data-table data-table--compact">
                        <thead><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>√(−1)</td><td>i</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>√(−4)</td><td>2i</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>√(−9)</td><td>3i</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>√(−25)</td><td>5i</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>√(−49)</td><td>7i</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <h3 class="article-h3">Cube Roots of Negative Numbers — Always Real</h3>
                <div class="math-block"><span class="math-formula">∛(−x) = −∛x</span></div>
                <div class="table-scroll-wrapper">
                    <div class="table-scroll-hint">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 8L22 12L18 16"/><path d="M6 8L2 12L6 16"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/></svg>
                        Scroll horizontally →
                    </div>
                    <table class="data-table data-table--compact">
                        <thead><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>∛(−8)</td><td>−2</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>∛(−27)</td><td>−3</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>∛(−125)</td><td>−5</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>∛(−1000)</td><td>−10</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>∛(−50)</td><td>≈ −3.684</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>No imaginary numbers needed — the racine cubique always stays in the real number system.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

