                <h2 class="article-h2">Real-Life Applications of Racine Carrée and Racine Cubique</h2>

                <div class="applications-grid">
                    <div class="app-card">
                        <div class="app-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="2" width="16" height="20" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="9" y1="22" x2="9" y2="2"/><line x1="15" y1="22" x2="15" y2="2"/><line x1="4" y1="8" x2="20" y2="8"/><line x1="4" y1="16" x2="20" y2="16"/></svg></div>
                        <h4>Architecture & Construction</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Room diagonal (√):</strong> A 10×10 m room has diagonal √(10²+10²) = √200 ≈ 14.14 m</li>
                            <li><strong>Cube side from volume (∛):</strong> A 1,000 m³ storage cube has sides of ∛1000 = 10 m</li>
                            <li><strong>Roof rafter length:</strong> √(rise² + run²) — Pythagorean theorem</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="app-card">
                        <div class="app-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="10" ry="4"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="10" ry="4" transform="rotate(60 12 12)"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="10" ry="4" transform="rotate(120 12 12)"/></svg></div>
                        <h4>Physics</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Velocity from KE (√):</strong> v = √(2KE/m)</li>
                            <li><strong>Sphere radius from volume (∛):</strong> r = ∛(3V/4π)</li>
                            <li><strong>RMS voltage (√):</strong> V_RMS = V_peak / √2</li>
                            <li><strong>Pendulum period (√):</strong> T = 2π√(L/g)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="app-card">
                        <div class="app-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"/><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"/><line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"/></svg></div>
                        <h4>Statistics & Data Science</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Standard deviation (√):</strong> σ = √[Σ(x − μ)²/N]</li>
                            <li>Powers polling margins, A/B test significance, quality control, and every bell curve</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="app-card">
                        <div class="app-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="23"/><path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg></div>
                        <h4>Finance & Investment</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Annual volatility (√):</strong> σ_annual = σ_daily × √252</li>
                            <li><strong>Geometric mean return (∛):</strong> ∛[(1+r₁)(1+r₂)(1+r₃)] − 1</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="app-card">
                        <div class="app-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 12h-4l-3 9L9 3l-3 9H2"/></svg></div>
                        <h4>Medicine</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Body surface area (√):</strong> BSA = √[(height × weight)/3600]</li>
                            <li><strong>Allometric dosing (∛):</strong> Dose ∝ Weight^(2/3)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="app-card">
